{{Short description|Opinion polling for the 61st Okaiken general election}}

'''Opinion polling for the [[Okaiken general election, 2026|61st Okaiken general election]]''' began following the [[Okaiken general election, 2025|60th general election]] in October 2025 and has continued through the campaign period leading up to the 17 May 2026 election.

The election was triggered by the collapse of the [[Honda-Nakayama Cabinet]] following the [[Nakayama Station dragging incident]] and the subsequent "March Maelstrom" civil unrest. Polling has tracked a dramatic realignment of Sanese politics, with the [[Okaiken Socialist Party]] (OSP) surging from 10.5% in the 2025 election to over 30% in April 2026, while the incumbent [[Progressive Party of Okaiken]] (PPO) has collapsed from 38.2% to the low 20s.

The late-campaign leadership change in the [[Sanese Communist Party]] (SCP)—with [[Kousuke Ikazaki]] replacing [[Shintaro Hamabe]] on 27 April 2026—produced a significant polling shift, with the SCP recovering from a collapse to 4.9% to a post-debate surge of 11.8%.

