==Key polling events==

===March Maelstrom impact===
The [[Nakayama Station dragging incident]] on 1 March 2026 and the subsequent "March Maelstrom" civil unrest produced the most dramatic polling shift of the campaign. Prior to the incident, the PPO held a lead of approximately 15–18 percentage points. Within three weeks, the party had collapsed to third place, with the OSP surging from the low 20s to over 30%.

The PPO's decline accelerated after Prime Minister Honda's 4 March Diet defense of one-man train operations, in which he stated that the country must accept "certain operational adjustments to maintain fiscal discipline." This statement was widely interpreted as prioritizing efficiency over safety, leading to the opposition slogan {{Nihongo|"Modernization over Mortality"|近代化より命|Kindaika yori Inochi}}.

===Ikazaki surge and post-debate shift===
The 27 April 2026 ouster of [[Shintaro Hamabe]] as SCP leader and his replacement by [[Kousuke Ikazaki]] produced a significant late-campaign polling shift. Ikazaki's "strength through discipline" messaging and surgical attacks on Nakayama's policy vagueness resonated with voters who had been attracted to the OSP's energy but questioned its readiness for governance.

The first televised debate on 30 April 2026, moderated by [[Ryuki Fukumoto]], further accelerated this shift. Post-debate polling showed:
* SCP: 7.2% → 11.8% (+4.6 points)
* OSP: 30.8% → 28.4% (−2.4 points)
* LDP: 28.5% → 27.1% (−1.4 points)
* PPO: 22.5% → 21.2% (−1.3 points)

The debate performance established Ikazaki as a credible alternative for left-wing voters skeptical of Nakayama's inexperience, while Nakayama's perceived "petulance" during exchanges with Honda alienated some moderate voters.

